1
00:01:30,458 --> 00:01:31,750
You are beating a police?

2
00:01:32,916 --> 00:01:35,666
You scumbag!
What were you thinking? To hit police.

3
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:37,125
How dare you strike at police?

4
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:38,583
Hold him tight.

5
00:01:38,750 --> 00:01:40,666
Scoundrel!
How could you hit police?

6
00:01:40,791 --> 00:01:41,958
What was on your mind?

7
00:01:41,958 --> 00:01:43,041
How old do you think you are?

8
00:01:58,916 --> 00:02:00,500
Bloody dog!

9
00:02:14,083 --> 00:02:15,375
There is no entry in the book, right?

10
00:02:19,541 --> 00:02:20,958
Hmm...
Let's do it.

11
00:02:23,041 --> 00:02:25,458
First, we have to give him good.

12
00:02:36,166 --> 00:02:38,416
Hey, can't you see?
I'm eating.

13
00:02:39,125 --> 00:02:40,250
You dropped my food.

14
00:02:40,583 --> 00:02:41,708
Do you think you are at home?

15
00:02:42,208 --> 00:02:43,291
To eat and relax.

16
00:02:44,458 --> 00:02:45,500
Wasn't lastnight enough?

17
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:47,250
Hey, what are you saying?

18
00:02:47,291 --> 00:02:49,291
We are in your area by accident.

19
00:02:49,458 --> 00:02:53,000
Had we been at Dhoolpet station,
they'd treat us with drinks and snacks.

20
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,833
That's who Don Chintu is!
Do you get it?

21
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,375
Right.
You get it?

22
00:02:57,708 --> 00:02:58,291
Is it?

23
00:02:58,625 --> 00:03:02,250
We too would like to spoil your boss, Chintanna.
Should we?

24
00:03:02,541 --> 00:03:03,625
Aye!

25
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,250
Keep quiet.
Leave it.

26
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,041
You please carry on.

27
00:03:15,458 --> 00:03:18,000
Beaten to pulp
yet this fool is smiling.

28
00:03:18,916 --> 00:03:21,041
He looks like a pothead.

29
00:03:21,375 --> 00:03:22,541
What do you smoke?

30
00:03:22,875 --> 00:03:24,833
Is it sweet or sour?

31
00:03:25,041 --> 00:03:25,666
Tell me.

32
00:03:25,708 --> 00:03:27,833
Hey, it's not sweet or sour.

33
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,291
I will tell you.

34
00:03:33,541 --> 00:03:35,666
He is drunk in love.

35
00:03:36,375 --> 00:03:38,958
It is an intoxication without cure.

36
00:03:39,125 --> 00:03:40,041
Love drunk?

37
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:43,625
How can you determine the issue
so easily, Chintanna? Wow!

38
00:03:43,708 --> 00:03:46,125
He is quite capable of it.

39
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:50,125
He can tell about a guy from his face
and a woman from her grace...

40
00:03:50,458 --> 00:03:52,166
-He can look and tell.
-That's right.

41
00:03:54,458 --> 00:03:57,541
In that case, brother,
can you read mine?

42
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,458
You stupid piece of shit!

43
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,750
Are you a woman?
You rogue!

44
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:06,666
Let him talk, not me.

45
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:11,000
Hey, brother, tell everyone
about your love story.

46
00:04:19,583 --> 00:04:20,833
Go on, share it.

47
00:04:22,083 --> 00:04:25,000
-There is no love story.
-Come on, tell us about it.

48
00:04:25,166 --> 00:04:26,958
Brother is asking.
Spill the beans.

49
00:04:27,041 --> 00:04:28,500
-Tell us, dear.
-Please brother.

50
00:04:28,541 --> 00:04:29,833
Let out now.

51
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:30,833
Hey, tell us.

52
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:31,916
Chintanna is asking.
Share it with us.

53
00:04:32,541 --> 00:04:35,708
Hey, there is no love story
as you are thinking.

54
00:04:36,875 --> 00:04:38,083
Hey, hey, hey.

55
00:04:38,458 --> 00:04:39,625
Okay, okay, okay.

56
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,166
I will tell.

57
00:04:47,791 --> 00:04:50,500
Since childhood, I’ve been captivated by beauty.

58
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,583
Cigarettes and alcohol, maybe not…

59
00:04:53,083 --> 00:04:54,416
but when it comes to beauty, we’re addicted.

60
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:58,333
Hey, you guys might think this is all
pretty common for a 20-year-old guy.

61
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:01,583
But for me, it’s something else entirely…
it feels like an addiction.

62
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:02,958
When it comes to beauty…

63
00:05:06,791 --> 00:05:09,750
Every morning I wake up just to cook,
pack lunch, carry water...

64
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:12,375
I break myself doing everything.
But no one cares.

65
00:05:12,458 --> 00:05:14,125
Look at him... not a care in the world.

66
00:05:15,625 --> 00:05:17,458
Just on his phone all the time.

67
00:05:17,625 --> 00:05:19,166
Goes out with his boys...

68
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:20,625
And get into unnecessary fights.

69
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:22,666
Doesn't ever both to help.

70
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:25,125
Hey!

71
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,583
Why don't you fetch some water?

72
00:05:28,375 --> 00:05:30,208
No way, dad.
You do it!

73
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:32,833
It's all just uncles and aunties carrying water.

74
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:34,833
My legs are really hurting anyway.

75
00:05:34,958 --> 00:05:36,166
I couldn't sleep all night.

76
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:37,166
Why didn't tell me?

77
00:05:37,541 --> 00:05:38,708
Why are your legs hurting?

78
00:05:38,958 --> 00:05:39,916
Let me massage.

79
00:05:39,958 --> 00:05:40,916
Place your legs here.

80
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,416
No need to massage, just sit on them
for a bit.

81
00:05:43,583 --> 00:05:44,416
Hmm.

82
00:05:45,041 --> 00:05:46,208
Put some weight and sit.

83
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:49,333
-Ah…
-Why are you groaning like an old guy?

84
00:05:51,041 --> 00:05:52,000
Oh!

85
00:05:52,375 --> 00:05:54,208
I wear myself out pressing his legs,

86
00:05:54,208 --> 00:05:56,750
-and you're making him press your's?
-This lady is always disturbing me.

87
00:05:57,083 --> 00:05:57,958
What a guy!

88
00:06:00,375 --> 00:06:01,833
Daddy, sit properly!
Can you?

89
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:03,125
Use more weight.

90
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:05,625
Wow!

91
00:06:08,291 --> 00:06:13,125
And the award for the best father goes to..
Mr. Shekhar.

92
00:06:13,875 --> 00:06:14,625
Wow!

93
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:17,500
-Aunty...
-Yes?

94
00:06:17,583 --> 00:06:19,125
The water flow has dropped.

95
00:06:25,458 --> 00:06:26,750
-Huh?
-Give it to me.

96
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,750
Go and take some rest.

97
00:06:30,583 --> 00:06:32,250
You should tell me
when there's work, Mom.

98
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:34,583
Why exhaust yourself?
I will take care of it.

99
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:49,375
“Any little bug that crawls into my head
turns my focus completely toward the ladies”

100
00:06:51,041 --> 00:07:03,791
“Even a glimpse of delicate feet adorned with toe rings
sends my heart completely out of control”

101
00:07:04,958 --> 00:07:09,208
“The more I grow,
the more my fascinations revolve around beauty"

102
00:07:09,208 --> 00:07:10,750
Why didn't you call me?

103
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:12,583
Oh!
Your clothes will get wet.

104
00:07:12,625 --> 00:07:13,833
-Aren’t you getting late?
-It’s okay.

105
00:07:13,833 --> 00:07:17,625
I’ll go now. Come.
"My roaming eyes keep finding their way to beauty"

106
00:07:18,875 --> 00:07:20,958
What a lucky guy!
This short guy.

107
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:24,875
Oh! He is here.

108
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:27,666
Are you done?

109
00:07:28,708 --> 00:07:29,625
Let's go.

110
00:07:29,958 --> 00:07:31,000
Hey, Vikrant.

111
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:32,208
Wait a minute.
Coming.

112
00:07:36,375 --> 00:07:37,416
He is Ram Singh.

113
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:38,750
Vikram's elder brother.

114
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,666
He is the president of the Miser’s Association.

115
00:07:42,958 --> 00:07:43,708
What is it?

116
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,333
Take this Rs.5 and go to the shop.

117
00:07:46,583 --> 00:07:51,625
And bring me a packet of incense, camphor,
turmeric powder, vermilion...

118
00:07:51,625 --> 00:07:53,875
..and a little oil and a banana.
Go and get it.

119
00:07:53,958 --> 00:07:55,333
Get all this in Rs.5?

120
00:07:55,333 --> 00:07:56,583
Or should I give you Rs.100?

121
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:58,916
Are you praying or trying to confuse me?

122
00:07:58,916 --> 00:08:01,083
Yeah right!
You tell me what I should do.

123
00:08:01,291 --> 00:08:02,166
You go and get it.

124
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:05,416
Doesn't earn a penny
but he is full of pride.

125
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:13,208
-Daddy.
-Hmm..

126
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:14,750
Should I drop you?

127
00:08:15,083 --> 00:08:15,958
Why bother?

128
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:19,208
You probably have a hundred things
to take care of. Carry on.

129
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:21,458
-Greetings, Shekhar brother.
-Hi there.

130
00:08:21,666 --> 00:08:22,625
Going to the shop?

131
00:08:23,416 --> 00:08:25,083
Where else? Can't avoid.

132
00:08:25,791 --> 00:08:26,958
Are you going to the office?

133
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:29,500
No, I've an earring.
I'll go to court and then to office.

134
00:08:30,875 --> 00:08:32,083
-Greetings, Lal.
-Greetings.

135
00:08:35,916 --> 00:08:37,375
What's up, hero?

136
00:08:43,458 --> 00:08:45,833
Damn!
God bless your sweet romance.

137
00:08:46,166 --> 00:08:47,333
Did you see that guy, Lal?

138
00:08:49,083 --> 00:08:51,125
All his eyes are on you
like a watch dog.

139
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:53,916
He is not just a retired police constable.

140
00:08:54,291 --> 00:08:55,708
He is a retired police dog.

141
00:08:58,250 --> 00:08:59,541
Wonder what he is up to.

142
00:08:59,541 --> 00:09:00,541
-Let's go.
-Okay.

143
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:12,666
Hey, fatso.

144
00:09:14,541 --> 00:09:15,333
What's up?

145
00:09:15,916 --> 00:09:16,875
Are you carrying?

146
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,916
Sure.
I'm in my 7th month.

147
00:09:20,125 --> 00:09:21,541
Throw me a baby shower.

148
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:23,000
Why should we?

149
00:09:23,041 --> 00:09:24,208
Ask the one who did it.

150
00:09:24,291 --> 00:09:26,750
-Hmm! Aren’t you the one who did it?
-Get lost. Move.

151
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,000
-Am I wrong?
-Get on.

152
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,541
Hey! What is it with him?

153
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,791
Why is he shaving everyday?

154
00:09:33,666 --> 00:09:34,750
-Mom.
-Hmm.

155
00:09:34,875 --> 00:09:35,708
What is this?

156
00:09:36,208 --> 00:09:37,166
Tell him please.

157
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,666
To stop this 'ex-mission' everyday.

158
00:09:40,541 --> 00:09:42,750
Hey! It is not ex-mission.

159
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,333
It is exhibition.

160
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,666
You are good for nothing.

161
00:09:46,458 --> 00:09:48,875
-Mom took off.
-All three of you have no shame.

162
00:09:48,875 --> 00:09:50,291
-Get on.
-How can you say that to him?

163
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,000
Calling it an exhibition...

164
00:09:52,666 --> 00:09:55,208
These are the friends I have had
since my birth.

165
00:09:55,541 --> 00:09:57,458
Although we are three, we are one soul.

166
00:09:57,833 --> 00:10:00,250
We have two bikes
but we ride together on one.

167
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:03,208
We share our tea too.
One by three.

168
00:10:10,333 --> 00:10:12,958
Sitting here everyday,
we turned this cafe into a casino.

169
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,208
We used this matchbox for gambling.

170
00:10:16,958 --> 00:10:19,333
These are the crooks in our stress free life.

171
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:21,791
They are Tony's boys.

172
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:24,125
Always up to no good.

173
00:10:24,708 --> 00:10:26,791
One day, we will smash them.

174
00:10:34,208 --> 00:10:37,333
Here you go.
Jackpot!

175
00:10:42,125 --> 00:10:43,625
Bro...

176
00:10:46,166 --> 00:10:47,125
It fell.

177
00:10:48,541 --> 00:10:50,416
Wow!

178
00:10:51,208 --> 00:10:51,958
Yay!

179
00:10:52,458 --> 00:10:55,375
This is what you call a jackpot.

180
00:10:55,833 --> 00:10:56,791
He blew on it.

181
00:10:57,333 --> 00:10:58,916
Collect the money.
Take it.

182
00:10:58,916 --> 00:11:00,041
He blew it down.

183
00:11:00,375 --> 00:11:02,250
Hey, what are you saying?!

184
00:11:02,375 --> 00:11:05,791
-Oh, damn...
-He blew on it and I saw him do it.

185
00:11:05,875 --> 00:11:08,333
You try to cheat me?
You rascal!

186
00:11:08,375 --> 00:11:09,958
Hands off him, you idiot!

187
00:11:10,083 --> 00:11:12,250
-What is this?
-Hold him down.

188
00:11:12,250 --> 00:11:14,625
Come here, you fatso.
Where are you running?

189
00:11:14,791 --> 00:11:16,875
Hey, hey! The police are here.
Please watch out.

190
00:11:17,041 --> 00:11:18,500
Let go of him.
Leave.

191
00:11:20,041 --> 00:11:21,083
Get lost.

192
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:27,166
You started the fight.

193
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:29,791
And you're sitting here peacefully.

194
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,208
If you’re afraid,
why pick a fight?

195
00:11:32,208 --> 00:11:34,708
If I beat them,
my punches will kill them.

196
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:36,333
Beat what?

197
00:11:37,166 --> 00:11:38,458
Hey! Shut up.

198
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,916
You guys use fights just to pass time.

199
00:11:43,416 --> 00:11:45,958
One day when your heads get cracked,
you'll understand.

200
00:11:46,458 --> 00:11:47,666
They are rowdies.

201
00:11:47,916 --> 00:11:49,041
Why do you bother them?

202
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:55,000
You should enjoy your college days
and set your life.

203
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:56,666
Idiots.

204
00:11:57,791 --> 00:11:59,333
Always getting into petty trouble.

205
00:12:02,375 --> 00:12:03,458
Oh no!

206
00:12:04,541 --> 00:12:05,708
Go away.

207
00:12:07,583 --> 00:12:09,375
He is leaving.
Fine, let him go.

208
00:12:09,958 --> 00:12:10,916
Munna...

209
00:12:12,458 --> 00:12:13,958
Aunty must have messaged him.

210
00:12:14,541 --> 00:12:15,416
This is the story.

211
00:12:15,875 --> 00:12:17,291
Cigarettes, alcohol and fights.

212
00:12:17,791 --> 00:12:20,166
I thought this is all my life will be.

213
00:12:21,166 --> 00:12:25,500
Then one day arrived and turned
my life upside down.

214
00:12:36,541 --> 00:12:45,291
“Hail, Hail Ganapati
Ganapati Bappa Morya!”

215
00:12:56,083 --> 00:13:01,708
“Hail Ganapati
Ganapati Bappa Morya!”

216
00:14:23,916 --> 00:14:26,833
My heart knew there was no one more beautiful
than her in the world.

217
00:14:27,291 --> 00:14:30,625
Day and night,
I was lost in her thoughts.

218
00:14:38,708 --> 00:14:45,916
"Something is beginning...
my body no longer feels at ease"

219
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:53,125
"Shall I see you fully, at least once?"

220
00:14:54,125 --> 00:14:57,958
"My lips won’t open properly,
like a trembling sigh"

221
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,541
"A flash of lightning has struck my heart"

222
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:09,500
"Is this love? Is this love?"

223
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:14,750
"Is this what stirs such turmoil in my heart?"

224
00:15:14,791 --> 00:15:19,041
"Is this love? Is this love?"

225
00:15:19,083 --> 00:15:26,500
"An unseen battle rages within,
while rain pours inside my chest"

226
00:15:26,708 --> 00:15:29,625
"There it is,
my heart said and rushed forward"

227
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:33,458
"Innocently, it collided, burned
in a whirlwind of confusion"

228
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:37,250
"I stumbled, searched,
and wandered longing to see you"

229
00:15:37,291 --> 00:15:41,125
"A melody, overwhelming and swift...
A tenderness I had never known before"

230
00:15:41,166 --> 00:15:45,000
"A waterfall of floods of light
A playful dance for eyes that had never met"

231
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:49,416
"The rising beauty reveals its own story
The very first springtime of love"

232
00:16:14,333 --> 00:16:22,333
"Perhaps she is here somewhere…
Somewhere here... "

233
00:16:22,416 --> 00:16:29,500
"Perhaps she cannot be seen...
O heart… my heart…"

234
00:16:29,625 --> 00:16:35,833
"In this hidden game, in the play of my heart…"

235
00:16:35,875 --> 00:16:41,625
"Your image, your thoughts,
return again and again"

236
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:46,916
"A moment that joins like
a spark feels like a blessing"

237
00:16:46,958 --> 00:16:52,166
"The weight of joyful dreams eventually tires,
scatters, and dissolves into restless chaos"

238
00:16:52,166 --> 00:16:56,000
"Once found, may we never part
with our lives tied together"

239
00:16:56,041 --> 00:16:59,833
"Let us stay united forever and
turn these timeless moments into our past"

240
00:16:59,875 --> 00:17:03,916
"Let our hearts find rhythm and union
Let the coming ages belong to us"

241
00:17:04,666 --> 00:17:08,041
"Something is beginning..."

242
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:11,833
"My body no longer feels at ease"

243
00:17:11,875 --> 00:17:18,916
"Shall I see you fully, at least once?"

244
00:17:20,041 --> 00:17:23,833
"My lips won’t open properly,
like a trembling sigh"

245
00:17:23,875 --> 00:17:29,458
"A flash of lightning has struck my heart"

246
00:17:31,208 --> 00:17:35,375
"Is this love? Is this love?"

247
00:17:35,375 --> 00:17:40,666
"Is this what stirs such turmoil in my heart?"

248
00:17:40,708 --> 00:17:44,958
"Is this love? Is this love?"

249
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:52,250
"An unseen battle rages within,
while rain pours inside my chest"

250
00:17:52,333 --> 00:18:01,208
“Is this love, is this love
the feeling that stirs a storm within my heart?”

251
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:05,666
“Is this love, is this love…”

252
00:18:06,083 --> 00:18:13,875
"An unseen battle rages within,
while rain pours inside my chest"

253
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:43,333
Go to MeeSeva centre and pay the current bill.

254
00:18:43,625 --> 00:18:45,333
What's wrong with you, Dad?

255
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:49,500
Is MeeSeva open on Sunday?
I don't even know what it is.

256
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:52,416
How can you be like this?

257
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:54,208
You can't even do basic errands.

258
00:18:54,708 --> 00:18:56,791
How will you survive when I'm dead?

259
00:18:57,166 --> 00:18:58,375
It is scary to think.

260
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,541
You are the only child.

261
00:19:00,833 --> 00:19:03,625
So what if I am the only child?

262
00:19:04,041 --> 00:19:06,791
If there were ten of us,
we’d all be playing cricket on the ground.

263
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:07,958
All age groups.

264
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,750
What are you requesting him for?

265
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:11,333
Sit down.

266
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:14,500
I will show you how to send him.
Give.

267
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:17,291
What is your problem?

268
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:19,375
What cricket team are you talking about?
I'll slap you.

269
00:19:19,375 --> 00:19:22,208
Why does he keep saying
I’m an only child?

270
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:26,333
Spoiling my relaxed Sunday.

271
00:19:26,375 --> 00:19:28,625
Oh!
You are so sweet.

272
00:19:28,666 --> 00:19:31,208
Relaxing on a Sunday...
Don't you feel ashamed?

273
00:19:31,708 --> 00:19:33,625
Shouldn't he stay home even on Sundays?

274
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:35,833
Do we have nothing to do
but stare at you?

275
00:19:36,291 --> 00:19:37,875
You're on the streets everyday, anyway.

276
00:19:38,291 --> 00:19:40,125
Would it hurt to pay the bill just once?

277
00:19:40,291 --> 00:19:41,166
Mom, give it to me.

278
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:44,000
I am a slave in this house.

279
00:19:45,708 --> 00:19:47,791
No worker relaxes at home like royalty.

280
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,208
When do you let me relax?

281
00:19:51,875 --> 00:19:53,583
You turn off the fan everytime I sleep.

282
00:19:54,333 --> 00:19:55,458
From the moment I wake up,

283
00:19:55,458 --> 00:19:59,083
I carry water, pay bills,
and do all the household chores...

284
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,750
Bloody hell!

285
00:20:01,833 --> 00:20:04,291
That's why you have me.
A worker would've cost you.

286
00:20:05,541 --> 00:20:08,208
You see how he is talking.

287
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,500
Hey, hey...
Wait a minute.

288
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:14,208
Get me a packet of curd too.

289
00:20:15,291 --> 00:20:16,958
-I need it.
-I won't get it.

290
00:20:18,875 --> 00:20:20,041
Take from the neighbour.

291
00:20:20,416 --> 00:20:21,500
Fine, don't get it.

292
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:23,166
Why should I take from them?

293
00:20:44,833 --> 00:20:47,875
Oh gosh!
Why is everyone here?

294
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:51,291
Hey dear...

295
00:20:56,208 --> 00:20:56,791
What is this?

296
00:20:57,333 --> 00:20:57,875
Token.

297
00:20:58,250 --> 00:20:59,125
Go and sit there.

298
00:20:59,208 --> 00:21:01,458
Go to the counter when it's your turn.

299
00:21:02,291 --> 00:21:04,000
Your bald head…(muttering)

300
00:21:08,625 --> 00:21:09,583
This is pure torture.

301
00:21:15,125 --> 00:21:15,833
Hey, mom.

302
00:21:15,916 --> 00:21:16,583
What happened?

303
00:21:16,583 --> 00:21:17,666
What's with these annoying people?

304
00:21:18,166 --> 00:21:19,291
That's not your house.

305
00:21:19,333 --> 00:21:19,583
Sorry.

306
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:21,083
For everything to be handed to you.

307
00:21:21,875 --> 00:21:24,375
I can't do this, Mom.
You know how bad it is here?

308
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,125
Why are there so many people?

309
00:21:26,541 --> 00:21:27,291
Obviously.

310
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,750
Someone here handed me a token...

311
00:21:29,875 --> 00:21:31,125
Take it &amp; stay in line.

312
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:34,458
Mom, I am very hungry.

313
00:21:34,666 --> 00:21:35,333
I am coming home.

314
00:21:35,791 --> 00:21:36,416
You hang up.

315
00:22:12,208 --> 00:22:13,875
Next token number.

316
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:16,250
143

317
00:22:28,166 --> 00:22:29,166
Give me the token.

318
00:22:36,083 --> 00:22:36,958
Hey...

319
00:22:38,041 --> 00:22:38,666
That day...

320
00:22:40,291 --> 00:22:41,375
Is it really you?

321
00:22:41,916 --> 00:22:43,333
Yes, it's me.

322
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,458
Do you work here?

323
00:22:46,666 --> 00:22:47,541
No.

324
00:22:48,208 --> 00:22:50,916
The chair was empty so I came and sat down.

325
00:22:51,041 --> 00:22:52,208
-Oh!
-Get it?

326
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:54,333
How funny!

327
00:22:55,666 --> 00:23:00,125
I was wondering what this angel was doing
among these aunties.

328
00:23:00,625 --> 00:23:01,166
No mind.

329
00:23:01,208 --> 00:23:02,333
Angel?

330
00:23:06,375 --> 00:23:08,583
-You know I have seen you before.
-Is it?

331
00:23:09,208 --> 00:23:10,875
You've no idea
how I searched for you.

332
00:23:11,958 --> 00:23:14,500
I was also waiting for you
to come to me.

333
00:23:14,750 --> 00:23:16,500
Why didn't you tell me before?

334
00:23:17,208 --> 00:23:18,375
I would have come flying.

335
00:23:19,041 --> 00:23:20,416
Flying?

336
00:23:23,250 --> 00:23:24,416
Too much.

337
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,416
Token number 143

338
00:23:30,708 --> 00:23:31,541
I was dreaming?

339
00:23:31,541 --> 00:23:32,916
Token number 143

340
00:23:33,375 --> 00:23:34,083
Not here?

341
00:23:34,708 --> 00:23:35,541
143

342
00:23:36,708 --> 00:23:38,458
Where did you go?
Give me the token.

343
00:23:41,166 --> 00:23:41,916
Give me the bill.

344
00:23:52,083 --> 00:23:53,083
Amount to be paid 622.

345
00:24:01,291 --> 00:24:02,791
You should’ve carried change with you.

346
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,583
How can I provide change
if everyone brings 500?

347
00:24:06,875 --> 00:24:07,291
Tell me.

348
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:13,625
Next token number.

349
00:24:13,916 --> 00:24:14,833
144

350
00:24:16,291 --> 00:24:18,000
Do you not even
look at the customer?

351
00:24:23,833 --> 00:24:24,708
What is it, Sir?

352
00:24:25,208 --> 00:24:26,291
Do you have another bill?

353
00:24:28,916 --> 00:24:29,416
Sir?

354
00:24:30,833 --> 00:24:32,083
Do you have more bills?

355
00:24:32,333 --> 00:24:34,833
You remember me from that day
on Ganesh mela...

356
00:24:35,166 --> 00:24:36,208
Next token number!

357
00:24:36,916 --> 00:24:37,958
Please move.

358
00:24:39,625 --> 00:24:40,125
Madam...

359
00:24:43,833 --> 00:24:44,791
Can't you wait?

360
00:24:45,583 --> 00:24:46,541
What are you looking at?

361
00:24:47,583 --> 00:24:48,916
What was he saying?

362
00:24:49,916 --> 00:24:52,875
He wants me to look at him and settle his bill.

363
00:24:54,250 --> 00:24:56,875
Is this a marriage proposal,
to look at faces?

364
00:24:57,916 --> 00:24:58,958
Yeah right.

365
00:24:59,541 --> 00:25:00,875
Sunday 9 to 1.

366
00:25:02,208 --> 00:25:03,041
We are one.

367
00:25:03,958 --> 00:25:06,250
Monday to Saturday 9 to 6.

368
00:25:07,625 --> 00:25:08,666
We are fixed.

369
00:25:11,041 --> 00:25:11,791
Uncle...

370
00:25:13,541 --> 00:25:16,208
From today, this is my office
as much as yours.

371
00:25:17,083 --> 00:25:17,541
Yeah.

372
00:25:18,416 --> 00:25:20,083
You are my salary.

373
00:25:21,625 --> 00:25:22,250
Bye.

374
00:25:23,125 --> 00:25:24,208
Is he mad?

375
00:25:29,875 --> 00:25:30,583
Oh!

376
00:25:30,958 --> 00:25:32,708
Lord Vishnu is chilling.

377
00:25:33,416 --> 00:25:34,000
Okay.

378
00:25:35,041 --> 00:25:36,875
-Mommy... Just a second.
-What's it?

379
00:25:38,041 --> 00:25:39,416
Here is the curd you asked for.

380
00:25:39,833 --> 00:25:40,875
Keep it there.
Move.

381
00:25:41,458 --> 00:25:42,041
Okay.

382
00:25:42,166 --> 00:25:42,958
Relax.

383
00:25:44,833 --> 00:25:45,875
You have to tell me, Daddy.

384
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:48,583
If there is any work,
you have to tell me.

385
00:25:49,291 --> 00:25:50,208
Didn't I pay just now?

386
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:51,833
I can do it again.

387
00:25:52,541 --> 00:25:54,000
It's no big task.
Huh!

388
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:56,083
Come here.

389
00:25:58,583 --> 00:25:59,583
What is it, Mom?

390
00:26:01,791 --> 00:26:04,083
What's this?
What are you doing?

391
00:26:04,500 --> 00:26:05,833
She is checking

392
00:26:06,125 --> 00:26:08,500
if you were boozing
while paying the bill.

393
00:26:08,958 --> 00:26:11,500
What do you mean?
You think I drink?

394
00:26:11,625 --> 00:26:13,791
You sound out of character.

395
00:26:14,250 --> 00:26:16,583
Did you step on something?
Or are you possessed?

396
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,875
You always say I do nothing.

397
00:26:19,291 --> 00:26:21,291
When I do,
you two fool around with me.

398
00:26:21,958 --> 00:26:24,125
You people think I am joke,
living in this house.

399
00:26:24,833 --> 00:26:26,208
These are just errands.

400
00:26:26,750 --> 00:26:27,916
Find some real work.

401
00:26:28,208 --> 00:26:29,416
How long will you relax for?

402
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:34,666
Why do you always circle back
to me getting work?

403
00:26:34,791 --> 00:26:35,916
And what work do you mean?

404
00:26:35,958 --> 00:26:37,500
So petty.
At least call it a job.

405
00:26:38,666 --> 00:26:39,458
Uneducated.

406
00:26:39,750 --> 00:26:40,583
Tell her, Daddy.

407
00:26:41,541 --> 00:26:42,708
I will find something.

408
00:26:43,250 --> 00:26:45,333
Didn't you just call me possessed?

409
00:26:45,833 --> 00:26:47,375
It's going to take time.

410
00:26:50,458 --> 00:26:53,541
With my bamboo
I can beat any ghost out of you.

411
00:27:01,083 --> 00:27:02,291
Is it a CC copy?

412
00:27:05,875 --> 00:27:07,458
Is everything okay, Amulya?

413
00:27:16,708 --> 00:27:17,875
-Hey, get up.
-Move.

414
00:27:19,083 --> 00:27:20,541
-Get up.
-Move it I say.

415
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:24,750
I am asking you to get up.

416
00:27:25,666 --> 00:27:26,291
What's this?

417
00:27:28,041 --> 00:27:30,583
I came to check how long
the queue was.

418
00:27:30,666 --> 00:27:34,458
Sure, I can tell what line
you're trying to get cleared.

419
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:35,541
Get out from here.

420
00:27:35,791 --> 00:27:38,500
Only come with bills. Or else don't come.
Leave now.

421
00:27:38,791 --> 00:27:40,208
Take your hands off me.
I'm going.

422
00:27:43,416 --> 00:27:45,375
The groom has gotten his blessings.

423
00:27:47,166 --> 00:27:48,958
Don't know.
Why should I care?

424
00:27:50,083 --> 00:27:51,958
-He was staring at you...
-Date of birth?

425
00:27:53,458 --> 00:27:54,375
Me?

426
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,833
No, I meant, me.
He was looking at me.

427
00:27:57,291 --> 00:27:59,291
As a guard,
why aren't you standing at the door?

428
00:27:59,333 --> 00:28:00,333
You can't come here casually.

429
00:28:00,375 --> 00:28:01,541
You should come only with bills.
Move.

430
00:28:02,750 --> 00:28:03,875
I will still come.

431
00:28:04,333 --> 00:28:05,708
You will return with bills.

432
00:28:06,916 --> 00:28:08,541
You think I'm a nobody, right?

433
00:28:08,541 --> 00:28:10,000
I am backed by big people.

434
00:28:10,208 --> 00:28:12,291
Okay, let us see.

435
00:28:16,375 --> 00:28:18,625
Aunty, your power bill,
current bill, electricity bill...

436
00:28:19,208 --> 00:28:20,708
-All three are the same.
-Right.

437
00:28:20,708 --> 00:28:22,500
Water bill, tap bill, land bill...

438
00:28:22,541 --> 00:28:23,666
Whatever it is, we will pay.

439
00:28:24,166 --> 00:28:25,708
This is a social experiment.

440
00:28:25,916 --> 00:28:27,125
It is social service.

441
00:28:27,208 --> 00:28:28,666
It's social service. Right.

442
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:31,041
Bro...

443
00:28:32,458 --> 00:28:33,291
We'll come later.

444
00:28:33,541 --> 00:28:34,875
-Why?
-Let's go.

445
00:28:35,291 --> 00:28:36,916
-Social service?
-Yes.

446
00:28:37,083 --> 00:28:37,958
Or is it for a girl?

447
00:28:40,625 --> 00:28:41,375
Let's go, Vikram.

448
00:28:42,166 --> 00:28:43,333
He is one police dog.

449
00:28:43,375 --> 00:28:45,333
Greetings, Aunty Sana.
You got any bills?

450
00:28:45,375 --> 00:28:47,791
Who's bill? For what?
Get going.

451
00:28:48,625 --> 00:28:50,625
She has given you good.
Move it.

452
00:28:50,666 --> 00:28:52,916
What's this?
Go home and study.

453
00:28:52,958 --> 00:28:54,916
-Bill? I don't have any...
-Uncle...

454
00:28:58,333 --> 00:29:00,041
Bloody hell!

455
00:29:00,125 --> 00:29:02,166
Damn!
Why is your street like this?

456
00:29:02,583 --> 00:29:03,583
There is no respect here.

457
00:29:04,416 --> 00:29:05,458
Let us go to my area.

458
00:29:05,833 --> 00:29:07,333
They are respectful over there.

459
00:29:07,916 --> 00:29:08,375
Is it?

460
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:09,708
Come on then.

461
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:11,666
-Do they have power here?
-Hi aunty...

462
00:29:12,625 --> 00:29:13,250
Aunty...

463
00:29:14,083 --> 00:29:14,833
Just one minute.

464
00:29:15,583 --> 00:29:16,625
Aunty!

465
00:29:16,625 --> 00:29:17,916
Who is that wild bear?

466
00:29:17,916 --> 00:29:18,375
Shit

467
00:29:19,208 --> 00:29:20,000
Respect...

468
00:29:21,833 --> 00:29:22,416
Aunty...

469
00:29:22,583 --> 00:29:23,791
Do you have unpaid electricity bills?

470
00:29:24,166 --> 00:29:26,625
I have but I am not free.

471
00:29:26,833 --> 00:29:29,166
Oh!
I'm here to help, Aunty.

472
00:29:32,375 --> 00:29:33,083
Aunty...

473
00:29:34,125 --> 00:29:35,041
How long more?

474
00:29:35,125 --> 00:29:36,250
I'm looking for it.

475
00:29:41,250 --> 00:29:41,958
Aunty...

476
00:29:42,625 --> 00:29:44,125
Aunty, did you find it?

477
00:29:44,666 --> 00:29:45,875
Still searching.

478
00:29:47,708 --> 00:29:48,500
He cleaned up well.

479
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,083
I'm here to help, Aunty.

480
00:29:54,541 --> 00:29:55,416
God bless you!

481
00:29:55,916 --> 00:29:56,958
I'm here to help, Aunty.

482
00:30:02,416 --> 00:30:03,541
Check the money.

483
00:30:04,333 --> 00:30:05,208
What is it?

484
00:30:05,625 --> 00:30:06,500
I'm here to help, Aunty.

485
00:30:10,916 --> 00:30:11,458
Aunty...

486
00:30:12,208 --> 00:30:14,208
Do you have electricity bill due?
We will pay.

487
00:30:14,416 --> 00:30:15,833
I am not free to give.

488
00:30:15,875 --> 00:30:17,208
But he is here to help, Aunty.

489
00:30:17,250 --> 00:30:18,000
Hey...

490
00:30:18,208 --> 00:30:18,958
Don't you want the bill?

491
00:30:21,250 --> 00:30:24,166
-Wash me properly.
-Yes, I am pouring.

492
00:30:24,208 --> 00:30:26,208
All this for a girl.

493
00:30:26,958 --> 00:30:28,375
Come, have a taste.
Here.

494
00:30:34,625 --> 00:30:38,791
I will take care of these bills
and win over the girl.

495
00:30:43,083 --> 00:30:45,750
Damn it!
What an embarassing lot you are!

496
00:30:56,791 --> 00:30:57,750
Here is the baldy.

497
00:30:58,041 --> 00:30:58,833
Take this bill.

498
00:30:59,833 --> 00:31:02,166
You said you'll return with a lot of bills.

499
00:31:02,166 --> 00:31:03,041
Give me the token.

500
00:31:03,833 --> 00:31:04,916
One bill is what you got.

501
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:07,916
I will bring only one per day.

502
00:31:08,541 --> 00:31:09,500
Is there a problem?

503
00:31:10,208 --> 00:31:10,666
Give me.

504
00:31:13,625 --> 00:31:15,125
I don't have a problem.

505
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:17,666
Make sure you don't cause one.

506
00:31:23,125 --> 00:31:24,541
Token No.14

507
00:31:30,166 --> 00:31:31,166
He is not here.

508
00:31:33,916 --> 00:31:36,000
Add 10 to that and it'll be 24.

509
00:31:36,708 --> 00:31:37,458
Can't you add?

510
00:31:37,458 --> 00:31:38,333
Token No.14

511
00:31:38,541 --> 00:31:39,000
Hello.

512
00:31:39,458 --> 00:31:40,041
My number.

513
00:31:40,833 --> 00:31:41,625
Sir, token.

514
00:31:41,625 --> 00:31:43,916
So tiny!
Why are you at this counter?

515
00:31:44,208 --> 00:31:44,833
Hey...

516
00:31:45,208 --> 00:31:46,375
Watch your mouth.

517
00:31:46,875 --> 00:31:48,000
-Sir, your bill?
-Hey, you.

518
00:31:48,916 --> 00:31:49,750
Give me your bill.

519
00:31:50,250 --> 00:31:51,333
She won't budge.

520
00:31:51,500 --> 00:31:52,166
-Are you sure?
-Sit.

521
00:31:52,333 --> 00:31:52,750
Come.

522
00:31:53,416 --> 00:31:53,958
Okay.

523
00:31:57,958 --> 00:31:59,500
You got to wait for you turn.

524
00:31:59,708 --> 00:32:00,375
Hello...

525
00:32:01,250 --> 00:32:02,750
You can't do as you please.

526
00:32:03,083 --> 00:32:03,958
Do you understand?

527
00:32:06,083 --> 00:32:07,083
Anyway...

528
00:32:07,541 --> 00:32:09,500
Aren't you looking enough at her from there?

529
00:32:10,250 --> 00:32:11,166
Up close...

530
00:32:11,333 --> 00:32:13,041
